    "body": "Part of #208. Owner acceptance and closure stay on that issue. The approved explicit Space cards action follows in a separate change.\n\nUndo and Redo keep fixed leading positions while history labels, save notices and connectivity change. Pressed styling preserves their target positions. The loaded editor owns one connection-status notice; the shell supplies it on loading, error and other routes.\n\nClaude Sonnet 5.5 xhigh implemented the UI after GPT architecture review. This candidate integrates the actual merged canvas predecessor #478 and targets main.\n\n## Candidate and verification\n\nHead `5a31678f5a8611ae3a89a1f6aefe797d7106a08e`, tree `c247968a388b1c74e7727ec27d4fe465ebfde0d0`, target main `1cfca9bce3967c9d41950266c83aab636667e0ab`. Final native source is `6b0eae62ea98ae73b22903c9922bba198e219608`; this publication commit changes only QA evidence and delivery metadata. Root verified all 531 new publication blobs and zero product or build-input changes. The 13 history product/test paths remain identical to the first reviewed candidate; inherited canvas product bytes match actual main.\n\n- Final integration passed 224 focused tests across 13 files on its first execution, plus typechecking, scoped lint and formatting. An earlier static evidence wrapper failed to retain the empty lint log; a static-only receipt pass established its exit code, without rerunning Vitest or changing source. Repository-wide formatting passed at publication. [Integration evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5a31678f5a8611ae3a89a1f6aefe797d7106a08e/docs/qa/2026-11-15-history-controls-final-integration/README.md)\n- A forced Node 22.23.4 build completed 12 tasks without cache hits. Independent GPT-6.1 Sol xhigh passed all 11 final native groups on their initial attempts, using Edge, the compiled gateway and disposable file SQLite. There were 77 stationary target windows, 21 trusted held presses and 66 exact conditional saves; four real 404 responses established settled error-route ownership. Zero page errors; all owned resources closed. No fixture corrections were used. [Final native evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5a31678f5a8611ae3a89a1f6aefe797d7106a08e/docs/qa/2026-11-15-history-controls-final-native/README.md)\n- Before/after bindings matched for 1,683 source paths, 27 embedded modules and 1,227 outputs across 13 distribution trees, with separate emitted-domain mapping. Root fully read the handoff, verified its 455 raw artifacts and the 475-file curated packet, and inspected representative native screenshots.\n\nThe original baseline, partial native runs, fixture failures and recovery are retained as historical evidence. The current complete matrix supersedes their coverage gaps without erasing them. Windows Edge automation, injected coarse touch and a DPR-2 reflow proxy do not establish physical touch, actual browser text zoom, screen-reader speech or other engines. Voice, authentication, storage/shutdown, StrictMode and renderer-error ownership retain focused component evidence.\n\n## Remaining gates\n\nThe first opposite-family review by GPT-6.1 Sol xhigh returned READY with no introduced blocker; [the full review](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/480#issuecomment-6887160473) remains part of the record. One of three total formal scans is used. Fresh CI at this publication head and the designated independent Astra max final audit are pending. Earlier stack CI is historical. The PR remains draft until those gates pass. No owner instance, store or service was changed.\n\n## Post-merge owner acceptance\n\nRecord the merged build and observations on #208:\n\n- Undo/Redo remain easy to find and target while editing, saving and changing connectivity.\n- The single connectivity notice and its placement are understandable on desktop and narrow layouts.\n- Pressed and disabled controls feel clear without unexpected movement.\n\nMachine-verifiable behavior remains the pipeline's responsibility; this checklist does not replace engineering gates.",
